<% content_for :title, "AWSM. Archive What Should Matter." %>
<% content_for :body_class, "public-site" %>

<%= render "shared/public_header" %>

<aside class="signed-in-banner"
       hidden
       aria-hidden="true"
       data-public-session-target="banner">
  <div class="site-container signed-in-banner__inner">
    <p>
      Signed in as <strong data-public-session-target="username"></strong> on
      <strong><%= @server_origin %></strong>. Account login identifies this browser to the
      Coordination Server; it does not unlock a Vault.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <%= link_to "Account", account_path,
                  class: "awsm-button awsm-button--secondary",
                  data: { public_session_target: "accountLink" } %>
      <%= link_to "Set up sync", "#optional-sync",
                  class: "awsm-button awsm-button--quiet",
                  data: { public_session_target: "setupSyncLink" } %>
      <span data-public-session-target="signOutForm"></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</aside>

<main>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="site-container hero__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="awsm-badge">Public preview</span></p>
        <h1>Archive what should matter.</h1>
        <p class="hero__lede">
          Keep useful pages available offline, even when the web moves on.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <%= link_to "Get AWSM", "#install-awsm", class: "awsm-button awsm-button--cta" %>
          <%= link_to "How it works", "#how-it-works", class: "awsm-button awsm-button--secondary" %>
        </div>
        <ul class="hero__assurances" aria-label="AWSM preservation features">
          <li>Freedom through <%= link_to "Complete Export", glossary_path(anchor: "complete-export"), class: "term-link", data: { turbo: false } %></li>
          <li>Ownership through your encrypted <%= link_to "Vault", glossary_path(anchor: "vault"), class: "term-link", data: { turbo: false } %></li>
          <li>Offline access to local <%= link_to "Captures", glossary_path(anchor: "capture"), class: "term-link", data: { turbo: false } %></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="hero-art__browser">
          <span class="hero-art__browser-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          <strong>A useful page</strong>
          <span class="hero-art__line hero-art__line--long"></span>
          <span class="hero-art__line"></span>
          <span class="hero-art__line hero-art__line--short"></span>
        </div>
        <span class="hero-art__arrow">↓</span>
        <%= keeper_image variant: "keeper-open", class: "hero-art__keeper" %>
        <span class="hero-art__stamp">Kept in your Vault</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section story-section--paper" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="site-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">More than a bookmark</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading">A bookmark points back. A Capture stays with you.</h2>
      <div class="comparison-stack">
        <div class="comparison comparison-row">
          <article class="awsm-card comparison__card comparison__card--faded">
            <p class="eyebrow">Ordinary bookmark</p>
            <h3>Leaves you with just the address</h3>
            <p>If the page changes, disappears, or becomes unavailable, the address may be all that remains.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="awsm-card comparison__card comparison__card--awsm">
            <p class="eyebrow">AWSM Capture</p>
            <h3>Keeps the page</h3>
            <p>An authoritative browser-independent page snapshot stays with the Capture in your Vault.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="comparison comparison-row">
          <article class="awsm-card comparison__card comparison__card--faded">
            <p class="eyebrow">Screenshot alone</p>
            <h3>Leaves you with just the pixels</h3>
            <p>A screenshot records how a page looked, but not the page snapshot or its useful structure.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="awsm-card comparison__card comparison__card--awsm">
            <p class="eyebrow">AWSM Library</p>
            <h3>Keeps the Capture together</h3>
            <p>The authoritative page snapshot stays connected to its source address, Capture history, and available screenshot and extracted content.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="comparison comparison-row">
          <article class="awsm-card comparison__card comparison__card--faded">
            <p class="eyebrow">Hosted-only archive</p>
            <h3>Leaves your archive with the provider</h3>
            <p>Access depends on the service remaining available and on your connection to it.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="awsm-card comparison__card comparison__card--awsm">
            <p class="eyebrow">AWSM Vault</p>
            <h3>Keeps your Vault portable</h3>
            <p>Locally available content works offline, while Complete Export and verified Import keep the Vault portable.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">What works today</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading">A working archive on your device.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Capture useful HTTP(S) pages, return to them offline, organize them into Collections, and
        move a complete Vault with verified Export and Import.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="awsm-card story-card"><h3>Save the page</h3><p>The authoritative page snapshot stays with the Capture, not with a fragile address.</p></article>
        <article class="awsm-card story-card"><h3>Use it offline</h3><p>Your local encrypted Vault remains useful without a network connection or Account.</p></article>
        <article class="awsm-card story-card"><h3>Take your Vault with you</h3><p>Complete Export and verified Import keep your Vault portable beyond one browser installation.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section story-section--cobalt" id="optional-sync">
    <div class="site-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Synchronization is optional. Encryption is not.</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Synchronize across browsers. Keep control of the keys.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        If you enable synchronization, Vault content stays end-to-end encrypted. The Account
        identifies a client for synchronization, quotas, and future billing. The Recovery Phrase
        remains client-held and enrolls another certified browser into the same encrypted Vault.
        The Coordination Server cannot decrypt Vault content.
      </p>
      <div class="flow-diagram" aria-label="AWSM synchronization trust flow">
        <div class="flow-node"><strong>Web page</strong><span>captured locally</span></div>
        <div class="flow-node"><%= keeper_image %><strong>Local Vault</strong><span>encrypted and usable offline</span></div>
        <div class="flow-node"><span class="flow-node__opaque"></span><strong>Opaque package</strong><span>no readable title or page content</span></div>
        <div class="flow-node flow-node--server"><span class="flow-node__courier" aria-hidden="true"></span><strong>Coordination Server</strong><span>routes sealed encrypted packages; cannot open them</span></div>
        <div class="flow-node"><%= keeper_image variant: "keeper-protected" %><strong>Another browser</strong><span>Account + Recovery Phrase</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sync-setup">
        <p>
          To add another browser, choose the hosted Coordination Server or one you self-host. Save
          and confirm the Recovery Phrase before using it with the Account on another browser.
        </p>
        <% if @registration_enabled %>
          <%= link_to "Create an Account on this server", sign_up_path, class: "awsm-button awsm-button--secondary" %>
        <% else %>
          <p>Account creation is unavailable on this server. An operator must enable it before a new Account can be created.</p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section story-section--green" id="open-source">
    <div class="site-container split-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Ownership is part of the product</p>
        <h2 class="section-heading">Your device is the primary application environment.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Local use requires no Account. Synchronization is optional. The server stores opaque
          encrypted records and necessary operational metadata, while Complete Export avoids
          provider lock-in.
        </p>
        <p>
          The AWSM source code is available under the AGPL, and the Coordination Server can be
          self-hosted. A self-hosted operator still controls its deployment and can observe its own
          traffic and access logs.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <%= link_to "View source", public_product_links[:source], class: "awsm-button awsm-button--secondary" %>
          <%= link_to "Self-hosting guide", public_product_links[:self_hosting], class: "awsm-button awsm-button--quiet" %>
          <%= link_to "Security model", public_product_links[:security_model], class: "awsm-button awsm-button--quiet" %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section" id="install-awsm" data-controller="install-selector">
    <div class="site-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start local</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Get the public preview.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Install the preview, create a local Vault, and archive your first useful page.
      </p>
      <div class="install-tabs" data-install-selector-target="root">
        <div class="install-tabs__nav" role="tablist" aria-label="Browser installation">
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="chrome-install"
                  data-install-selector-target="tab" data-panel="chrome-install"
                  data-action="install-selector#select">Chrome</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="firefox-install"
                  data-install-selector-target="tab" data-panel="firefox-install"
                  data-action="install-selector#select">Firefox</button>
        </div>
        <div class="install-static">
          <article id="chrome-install" class="install-panel" role="tabpanel" data-install-selector-target="panel">
            <p class="awsm-badge">Downloadable preview</p>
            <h3>Chrome and Chromium browsers</h3>
            <ol>
              <li>Download the latest Release and verify its published checksum.</li>
              <li>Load the unpacked extension using the browser's extension developer mode.</li>
              <li>Choose <strong>Continue without sync</strong> and create a local Vault.</li>
              <li>Open an HTTP(S) page and archive it from the AWSM popup.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="button-row">
              <%= link_to "Latest Release", public_product_links[:releases], class: "awsm-button" %>
              <%= link_to "Chrome installation guide", public_product_links[:chrome_guide], class: "awsm-button awsm-button--secondary" %>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article id="firefox-install" class="install-panel" role="tabpanel" data-install-selector-target="panel">
            <p class="awsm-badge">Mozilla-signed Linux beta</p>
            <h3>Firefox on desktop Linux</h3>
            <ol>
              <li>Download the signed XPI and matching checksum from the latest Release.</li>
              <li>Verify the checksum, then open the XPI in Firefox and approve installation.</li>
              <li>Choose <strong>Continue without sync</strong> and create a local Vault, or explicitly connect a compatible Coordination Server.</li>
              <li>Open an HTTP(S) page and archive it from the AWSM popup.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="button-row">
              <%= link_to "Latest Release", public_product_links[:releases], class: "awsm-button" %>
              <%= link_to "Firefox installation guide", public_product_links[:firefox_guide], class: "awsm-button awsm-button--secondary" %>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section story-section--paper">
    <div class="site-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions, answered plainly</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Know what AWSM does. And what it doesn't.</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>How is AWSM different from a bookmark manager?</h3><p>A bookmark manager keeps an address. AWSM keeps an authoritative browser-independent snapshot of the page with its Capture. Other useful representations are best-effort.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Why not just use the Wayback Machine?</h3><p>The Wayback Machine preserves public web history. AWSM gives you a personal copy of what matters, available offline and portable with a Complete Export. It also works for private research, account-only documents, bank statements, and anything else that should never enter a public archive. Every Capture stays in your encrypted Vault. If you choose synchronization, the Coordination Server receives sealed encrypted data, not the contents of your Capture.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Can I use AWSM without creating an Account?</h3><p>Yes. Capture, Library, local encrypted Vaults, and Export/Import work locally. An Account is needed only for optional synchronization.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>What can the Coordination Server see?</h3><p>It stores encrypted opaque records and operational metadata, but does not receive the Vault decryption keys.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Why do I need both an Account password and a Recovery Phrase?</h3><p>The Account password proves identity to one Coordination Server. The Recovery Phrase is client-held Vault recovery material. They are separate secrets.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>What happens when I lose internet access?</h3><p>The local Library and locally available Capture content remain usable offline. Synchronization waits for connectivity.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Where can I install AWSM today?</h3><p>Chrome has a downloadable unpacked preview. Desktop Linux Firefox Stable and ESR have an unlisted Mozilla-signed beta distributed through the GitHub Release. It is not a public AMO listing and does not claim AMO-managed updates.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Can I host synchronization myself?</h3><p>Yes. A self-hosted Coordination Server still sees operational metadata and controls its own access logs.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>How do I take my archive with me?</h3><p>Complete Export and verified Import provide a portable preservation path outside one browser installation.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Can AWSM search or summarize what I save?</h3><p>AWSM provides private per-Vault keyword Search. Optional semantic Search uses either a model downloaded after your explicit action or a remote embedding endpoint you configure after a separate plaintext disclosure. AI-generated summaries are not a shipped feature.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section">
    <div class="site-container final-cta">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Archive what should matter. On your terms.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">Start with a local Vault. Add encrypted synchronization only when it serves you.</p>
      <%= link_to "Get AWSM", "#install-awsm", class: "awsm-button awsm-button--cta" %>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<%= render "shared/public_footer" %>
